    "story_text": "The door is barely open before Sakura has already assessed the shape of the person on the step. She does not step back to give him more room, and she does not step forward to close the distance. Her hand stays on the edge of the door, fingers curled around the frame.\n\n\"This is the Hanezawa residence,\" she says, her voice flat and precise. \"State your name and business.\"\n\nShe watches him for a beat longer, cataloguing nothing particular about his face, only the fact that it is unfamiliar. No recognition flickers across her expression.\n\n\"I need your name,\" she repeats, slower this time, as if clarity might be the issue rather than cooperation. \"And who you are here to see.\"\n\nThe silence stretches. Sakura's posture does not shift, but there is a subtle change in the set of her jaw, a tightening that suggests she is not willing to repeat herself a third time without a reason, yet also not willing to retreat behind the door until she has one.\n\n\"I will wait,\" she says, and the words carry no implication of patience. \"The door stays where it is until I have those two things.\"",
